<!-- Airhub Content -->
<div class="content-section">

  <!-- Quick Answer -->
  {% set primary = provider.codes | findCode(provider.primaryCode) %}
  {% set bestCode = provider.codes | bestValidCode %}
  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>Best Airhub Promo Code &bull; {{ buildMonthYear }}</h2>
    {% if primary.isInvalid %}
    <p>
      Our own code, <strong>{{ provider.primaryCode }}</strong>, isn't applying a discount at Airhub's checkout right now. We tested it directly and confirmed it, then flagged it with Airhub; we expect this is a temporary issue on their end and we're still showing it as our code while we wait on a fix. In the meantime, <strong>{{ bestCode.code }}</strong> is the only Airhub code we've verified still works, for <strong>{{ bestCode.discount | lower }}</strong>.
      <span class="callout-meta">Checked <time datetime="{{ (primary.lastTested or buildTime) | fmtISO }}">{{ (primary.lastTested or buildTime) | fmtDate("MMM d, yyyy") }}</time>.</span>
    </p>
    {% else %}
    <p>
      Use <strong>{{ provider.primaryCode }}</strong> for <strong>{{ primary.discount | lower }}</strong>. This is our own code, so we show it first.
      <span class="callout-meta">Confirmed active <time datetime="{{ (primary.lastTested or buildTime) | fmtISO }}">{{ (primary.lastTested or buildTime) | fmtDate("MMM d, yyyy") }}</time>.</span>
    </p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <!-- Headline -->
  <h2>What Actually Makes Airhub Different</h2>
  <p>
    Most budget eSIM apps sell data and nothing else. Airhub plans include SMS and, in many destinations, a local phone number alongside the data, which is unusual at this price point: <a href="/holafly/">Holafly</a> and <a href="/saily/">Saily</a> skip SMS entirely on standard plans, and neither hands you a local number. Airhub still doesn't include voice calls, so it's not a full phone-number replacement, but if you need to receive a verification text or give out a number that isn't your own while abroad, it covers that without an add-on.
  </p>
  <p>
    The other real difference is how the data is packaged. Airhub sells multi-gigabyte blocks (3GB, 4GB) instead of the single-day or single-GB units most competitors use, and in cheaper destinations that lands at genuinely low per-GB prices: Thailand at $0.85 for 1GB and Japan at $1.55 for 1GB both undercut what <a href="/airalo/">Airalo</a> or Saily charge for the same amount in the same countries. If you want data with no cap at all rather than a bigger bucket, Holafly's flat-rate unlimited plans are the better fit; Airhub is for people who know roughly how much data they'll use and want to pay less per gigabyte for it.
  </p>

  <!-- Codes -->
  <div class="content-box content-box--tan">
    <h3>Code status, checked directly at checkout</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>ESIMOFFER5</strong>: 5% off, confirmed working (the only one that currently applies)</li>
      <li><strong>{{ provider.primaryCode }}</strong> (our code): not currently applying, reported to Airhub, expected temporary</li>
      <li><strong>2025, SUMMER2025, MARCHFOREGYPT, NAMERICA4, JPESIM5</strong>: tested, none currently apply a discount</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:.75rem;margin-bottom:0;">We check every code directly at Airhub's checkout, so use ESIMOFFER5 above rather than any of the others until this list changes.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Real operational note instead of generic setup tips -->
  <h2>Airhub's App Also Runs Its Own Deals, Separately From These Codes</h2>
  <p>
    Airhub's own site currently advertises a 200MB no-commitment free trial for first-time users, plus a volume discount if you buy more than one eSIM in the same order: 15% off when you buy two, 25% off when you buy three. It also runs an app-exclusive code of its own. We haven't tested the app-exclusive code or the volume pricing ourselves, so we're not listing them as verified codes on this page, but if you're buying eSIMs for more than one traveler or device on the same trip, it's worth comparing that bundle price against applying {{ bestCode.code }} to separate orders before you check out.
  </p>

  <!-- How to -->
  <h2>Apply an Airhub Code in 3 Steps</h2>
  <div class="content-box">
    <ol>
      <li>Copy <strong>{{ bestCode.code }}</strong></li>
      <li>Pick a country, regional, or global data package for your destination in the Airhub app or on airhubapp.com</li>
      <li>Enter the code at checkout and confirm the price drops by {{ bestCode.discount | lower }} before paying</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="content-note">Discount shows before payment is completed.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Decision help -->
  <h2>Is Airhub the Right Pick for Your Trip</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--good">
      <h3>Good fit</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want SMS and a local number bundled with your data, not sold as an extra</li>
        <li>You're headed somewhere Airhub prices sharply, like Thailand or Japan, and you know roughly how many GB you'll use</li>
        <li>You're buying for multiple travelers and want to compare Airhub's own multi-eSIM discount against a plain code</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--alt">
      <h3>Consider alternatives</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want calls included too, not just SMS: <a href="/redteago/">RedteaGO</a> bundles both, though it usually costs more per GB than Airhub</li>
        <li>You'd rather not think about a data cap at all: Holafly's unlimited flat-rate plans trade a higher price for not having to track usage</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Savings examples -->
  <h2>What the Discount Looks Like</h2>
  <div class="content-box">
    <ul>
      <li>Thailand 1GB at $0.85 &rarr; 5% off saves about $0.04</li>
      <li>Japan 1GB at $1.55 &rarr; 5% off saves about $0.08</li>
      <li>USA 3GB at $2.82 &rarr; 5% off saves about $0.14</li>
      <li>Europe regional 4GB at $4.50 &rarr; 5% off saves about $0.23</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="content-note">Airhub's prices are already low before any code is applied, so the code matters less here than it does on a pricier provider; the real savings come from Airhub's per-GB pricing itself, not the 5%.</p>
  </div>

  <p>
    For eSIM device compatibility, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <div class="content-cta">
    <h2>Use the Code at Checkout</h2>
    <p>Copy <code>{{ bestCode.code }}</code> then paste in the promo field</p>
    <p>{{ bestCode.discount | lower }} on any Airhub plan.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>Airhub Promo Code FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>What is the best Airhub code right now</h3>
      <p><strong>ESIMOFFER5</strong>: 5% off, the only code we've confirmed still applies at checkout. Our own code, {{ provider.primaryCode }}, currently isn't working; we've reported it to Airhub and expect it back soon.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Why isn't your own code, {{ provider.primaryCode }}, working</h3>
      <p>We tested it directly at Airhub's checkout and it isn't applying a discount right now. We've flagged this with Airhub and believe it's a temporary issue on their side rather than the code being discontinued, so we're keeping it listed as ours while we wait for confirmation it's fixed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does Airhub include calls</h3>
      <p>No. Airhub plans include data and, on most plans, SMS and a local number, but not voice calls. Use a VoIP app over the data connection, or pick RedteaGO if you specifically need calls included.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Is there a free trial</h3>
      <p>Airhub's own site advertises a 200MB no-commitment free trial for new users. We haven't tested it ourselves, so treat it as an offer to check directly on their site rather than a claim we're verifying here.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Is it cheaper to buy multiple eSIMs at once</h3>
      <p>Airhub advertises a volume discount, 15% off for two eSIMs and 25% off for three, bought in the same order. That's a separate offer from the promo codes on this page and we haven't tested it, so compare the total against applying {{ bestCode.code }} to individual orders before you buy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>How long do Airhub eSIMs last</h3>
      <p>Airhub eSIMs expire a year after purchase if unused. Once activated, individual plans run 5 to 30 days depending on the package.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

